mplementation and tests separate per the constraints. I'm laying out the specific requirements that need to be implemented—R3.1 through R3.4 from the SRD—and mapping them to implementation tasks in the expand command. The design decisions section is where I'd document the approach for handling these new requirements. I need to verify that the existing R1.1-R2.4 functionality remains intact with no regressions, then move on to implementing the R4.1-R4.3 requirements from the specification. I'm looking at the design decisions around how to implement the expand command—specifically using the differential testing utilities from the testutils package to validate the behavior against a reference binary, and ensuring any test requirements from the spec are incorporated into the test suite. I'm laying out the requirements and design decisions for building the unexpand utility—I need to create the main entry point with all the necessary flag parsing, helper function stubs, and SIGPIPE handling following the project's conventions and using expand as a structural reference. Looking at the requirements and design decisions for implementing the R1.1-R1.4 specifications from the SRD, I need to reference the exact spec details and follow the established patterns from the expand utility while adhering to project conventions. I'm reconsidering whether to include the test file in this task—the SRD requirements R4.x might actually specify testing, which would make expand_test.go the right file to include rather than main.go. Since I'm not certain what R4 contains, I should probably note both possibilities and let the agent decide based on the full SRD context. and tests. Let me verify the ordering constraint one more time: documentation before code, contracts before implementations, types before consumers, implementation before tests, with ties broken alphabetically by file path. The expand tasks come before unexpand tasks, R3 before R4 within expand, and contract before implementation within unexpand—so the sequence is correct. I should also make sure each task description is self-contained for the agent, explicitly noting that cmd/expand/main.go already contains the R1.1-R2.4 implementation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55368,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55368},"output_tokens":37,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb1d07d5-2d51-48e7-aa2b-abb96dd3160a","uuid":"3770e6f2-3dcb-4efe-9734-829a97535e53"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013U6Bt8pnKbUFEABLnP9iUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a specification-driven AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds one package per utility, `pkg/` holds shared libraries (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), `docs/specs/` holds SRDs and use cases, and `magefiles/` holds build automation.\n\n**Current state**: All 114 SRDs are written. Many utilities have been implemented in this generation run. The most recent commits implemented `cmd/expand` R1.1-R2.4. The `requirement_states` field shows which requirements are still \"ready\" (not yet implemented).\n\n**Current release**: The earliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **rel05.1** (expand/unexpand). Expand has R3.1-R4.3 remaining; unexpand has all 14 requirements (R1.1-R4.4) remaining.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 05.1 is the earliest release with ready requirements. Expand (srd024) has 7 remaining ready requirements (R3.1-R3.4, R4.1-R4.3). Unexpand (srd025) has 14 ready requirements (R1.1-R4.4). Expand already exists in source; unexpand is a new package requiring a contract task.\n\n## Weight Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd024-expand R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) + R3.4(1) = 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd024-expand R4.1(1) + R4.2(1) + R4.3(1) = 3 ✓\nTask 2: contract task, no SRD weight requirements\nTask 3: srd025-unexpand R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) = 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/expand: implement srd024-expand R3.1-R3.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd024-expand.yaml (requirements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4)\n      - cmd/expand/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1 through R2.4)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project conventions and build instructions)\n      - pkg/sys/ (for InstallSIGPIPEHandler convention)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/expand/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R3.1-R3.4 functionality to existing expand implementation\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R3.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R3.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R3.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R3.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read srd024-expand.yaml for the exact specification of R3.1-R3.4. Modify the existing cmd/expand/main.go -- do not rewrite from scratch. Preserve all existing R1.1-R2.4 functionality.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow existing code patterns in main.go for flag parsing, I/O handling, and error reporting.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Ensure sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at the start of main if not already present.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/expand ./cmd/expand/ succeeds\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/expand/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All behavior specified in srd024-expand R3.1-R3.4 is implemented in cmd/expand/main.go\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Existing R1.1-R2.4 functionality is preserved -- no regressions in flag parsing or tab expansion logic\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/expand: implement srd024-expand R4.1-R4.3\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd024-expand.yaml (requirements R4.1, R4.2, R4.3)\n      - cmd/expand/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1 through R3.4)\n      - cmd/expand/expand_test.go (existing test file, if present)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness -- BuildBinary, RunDiffTests, DiffTest)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project conventions, differential testing pattern, and build instructions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/expand/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R4.1-R4.3 functionality to complete the expand implementation\n      - path: cmd/expand/expand_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Create or update differential test file if R4.x requirements include testing\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R4.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R4.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd024-expand requirement R4.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read srd024-expand.yaml for the exact specification of R4.1-R4.3. Modify existing files -- do not rewrite from scratch.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"If R4.x includes differential test requirements, use the project testing pattern: testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\"), exec.LookPath(\\\"gexpand\\\"), t.Skip if not found, testutils.RunDiffTests with []testutils.DiffTest.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The reference binary for expand is gexpand (Homebrew GNU coreutils). Always call exec.LookPath and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/expand ./cmd/expand/ succeeds\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/expand/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All behavior specified in srd024-expand R4.1-R4.3 is implemented\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/expand/... -count=1 passes (tests skip gracefully if gexpand reference binary is not in PATH)\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/unexpand (contract)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml (full SRD -- all requirement groups R1 through R4)\n      - cmd/expand/main.go (reference for tab-conversion utility structure -- unexpand is the inverse of expand)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project conventions and build instructions)\n      - pkg/sys/ (for InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/unexpand/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Contract stub file with package declaration, imports, main function skeleton, flag definitions for all srd025-unexpand flags, and internal function signatures\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create cmd/unexpand/main.go with package main declaration and all imports needed by srd025-unexpand\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define the main function skeleton with sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), flag variable declarations for all flags in srd025-unexpand, and flag.Parse call\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define stub signatures for all internal helper functions needed by srd025-unexpand -- e.g., unexpand processing logic, tab stop list parsing, whitespace conversion\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"All function bodies contain minimal placeholder logic (e.g., return nil or os.Exit(0)) so the file compiles and builds\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read srd025-unexpand.yaml to identify all flags, modes, and behaviors. Create a stub for each distinct behavior.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use cmd/expand/main.go as structural reference -- unexpand shares tab stop configuration and I/O patterns with expand.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention for all cmd/ utilities that write to stdout.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/unexpand/main.go exists and compiles: go build -o bin/unexpand ./cmd/unexpand/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/unexpand/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All flags from srd025-unexpand have corresponding flag variable declarations\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"All internal helper functions have stub signatures -- the file is structured for incremental implementation of R1.1-R4.4\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/unexpand: implement srd025-unexpand R1.1-R1.4\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml (requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\n      - cmd/unexpand/main.go (contract stubs from previous task)\n      - cmd/expand/main.go (reference implementation for tab-conversion utility patterns)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project conventions and build instructions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/unexpand/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Implement R1.1-R1.4 by filling in contract stubs with working logic\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R1.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R1.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R1.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R1.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read srd025-unexpand.yaml for the exact specification of R1.1-R1.4. Fill in the stub functions from the contract task -- do not restructure the file.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"unexpand converts spaces to tabs. By default only leading whitespace is converted. Follow the SRD for exact conversion semantics.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Preserve all contract stubs for R2-R4 requirements -- only